-- EXPECT-ERROR: contains an `extern` block
-- Capabilities widening, Task 4 -- `cap no_extern` (`check_no_extern_module`,
-- `typecheck.ml:6231-6255`), the REJECT side: a `DExtern` block declared
-- inside a `cap no_extern` module. `check_no_extern_module`'s `DExtern` arm
-- (`:6235-6239`) raises unconditionally on any extern block regardless of
-- whether its own `Cap(X)`/`needs IO.Foreign` obligations (Checks 5/1c) are
-- otherwise satisfied -- `needs IO.FileSystem` here covers Check 5's own
-- `Cap(IO.FileSystem)` obligation cleanly (no unrelated diagnostic), so the
-- ONE error surfacing is `no_extern`'s own: `` `mod NoFFI` (declared `cap
-- no_extern`) contains an `extern` block (`libc`). ``. (A second, WARNING-
-- level Check 1c diagnostic -- "extern block ... requires `Cap(IO.Foreign)`
-- but `NoFFI` does not declare `needs IO.Foreign`" -- also fires alongside,
-- since this program does not separately declare `needs IO.Foreign`; it
-- does not change the exit code and is not the substring pinned here.) See
-- core-march-types.md §2.8.11.
mod NoFFI do
  cap no_extern
  needs IO.FileSystem

  extern "libc" : Cap(IO.FileSystem) do
    fn c_read(fd : Int, buf : String, n : Int) : Int
  end
end
